==Trivia==
*Euler Archipelago's name references Swiss mathematician, physicist, astronomer, geographer and engineer [[wikipedia:Leonhard Euler|Leonhard Euler]]. It may specifically be a reference to [[wikipedia:Euler's laws of motion|Euler's laws of motion]] that was lost in translation, as 運動 ''undō'' (motion) sounds similar to 群島 ''guntō'' (archipelago).

